// Hint, Borrow and Give lend a writer its buffer, as encoding/json keeps
// its encodeState in a pool: a writer that builds a text in a []byte
// borrows an empty buffer, appends to it, takes its text with FromBytes,
// and gives the buffer back for the next writer. Any module's writer may
// borrow (std json's Encode is one, a module's own codec another), so a
// text encoded again allocates its result and no buffer, whoever wrote
// the codec. Each writer type W writing a value type T has a size hint,
// the length of its last text, so a borrow after a GC emptied the pool
// allocates one buffer of that size, not a small one regrown.

// Hint is the size hint of a writer of type W writing a T, the handle its
// Borrow and Give take.
extern go ergo.local/prototype/runtime/v1.StringsHint func Hint[W, T]() int

// Borrow is an empty buffer of at least hint's size.
extern go ergo.local/prototype/runtime/v1.StringsBorrow func Borrow(hint int) []byte

// Give records out's length in hint, puts out's buffer back in the pool
// and gives out, so a writer gives its buffer back in place,
// `t.out = strings.Give(t.out, hint)`: nothing may read or write out
// after.
extern go ergo.local/prototype/runtime/v1.StringsGive func Give(out []byte, hint int) []byte

// FromBytes is the text of b, a copy of its bytes.
extern go ergo.local/prototype/runtime/v1.StringsFromBytes func FromBytes(b []byte) string
